<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.9.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00212</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.9.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2914145a-8df9-4c28-be5b-0d246c2d50b3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">For numbers 1 – 9, use the following scenario: A car has a 16-gallon fuel tank. When driven on a highway, it has a gas mileage of 30 miles per gallon. The gas mileage (also called "fuel efficiency") tells us the number of miles the car can travel for a particular amount of fuel (one gallon of gasoline, in this case). After filling the gas tank, the driver got on a highway and drove for a while.</para>
      <exercise id="c9c0b944-2eb3-43b2-acc4-79148148453b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">How many miles has the car traveled if it has 15 gallons left in the tank?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Correct! 30 miles</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00006">The correct answer is 30 miles.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0b8af3c9-6742-4109-9f34-7f7fab8f173e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">How many miles has the car traveled if it has 10 gallons left in the tank?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Correct! 180 miles</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is 180 miles.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_2ab2e5e8-03f0-40d4-898e-c6155a3fe6c4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">How many miles has the car traveled if it has 2.5 gallons left in the tank?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">Correct! 405 miles</para>
          <para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is 405 miles.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_97d672df-68be-43e5-8182-3eeb958b2ccd" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Choose the equation that represents the relationship between the distance the car has traveled in miles, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and the amount of gas left in the tank in gallons, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00016">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00017"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00018"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00020"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00021">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00022">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_6b70c89b-27d4-46db-830d-6009497c889c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00024">How many gallons are left in the tank when the car has traveled 90 miles?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00025">Correct! 13 gallons</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is 13 gallons.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0c673f94-e584-4e9e-a231-7697c0dba0dc" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00028">How many gallons are left in the tank when the car has traveled 246 miles?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00029">Correct! 7.8 gallons</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00031">The correct answer is 7.8 gallons.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3480b5d0-91da-4121-bd45-5ab49f90db3c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00032">Choose an equation that makes it easier to find the amount of gas left in the tank, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, if we know the car has traveled <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> miles.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00034"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00035"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00037"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00038">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00039">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00040">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>480</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c4617740-0dff-4561-ab05-fbbbcf1b0df6" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00041">Noah was helping to collect the entry fees at his school's football game. Student entry costs $2.75 each and adult entry costs $5.25 each. By the end of the game, Diego had collected $281.25.</para>
          <para id="para-00042"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> equations that could represent the relationship between the number of students, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the number of adults, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and the dollar amount collected at the game.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00043">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>281.25</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5.25</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2.75</m:mn><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>53.57</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2.75</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5.25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00045">The correct answers are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>281.25</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5.25</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2.75</m:mn><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>53.57</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2.75</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5.25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
